      <unicode>ᠶᠠᠯᠢᠬᠣ</unicode>
      <uighur>yaliqu</uighur>
      <cyrillic>ялих</cyrillic>
      <transcript>JALI-</transcript>
      <definition>v.i. To be in great quantity; to be of good quality.</definition>
      <page>426</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠶᠠᠯᠢᠬᠣ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>- -xu ygei</transcript>
          <definition> Small, insignificant, unimportant, it does not pay ( to do it), is not worth while.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠶᠠᠯᠢᠵᠤ ᠢᠳᠡᠭᠰᠡᠨ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>--zu idegsen ygei</transcript>
          <definition> Has or have not eaten much.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠴᠠᠰᠤ ᠶᠠᠯᠢᠭᠰᠠᠨ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>casu jaliγsan ygei</transcript>
          <definition> Only a little Snow has fallen.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠨᠡ ᠵᠢᠯ ᠮᠠᠯ ᠶᠠᠯᠢᠵᠤ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>ene zil mal --zu ygei</transcript>
          <definition> This year the cattle are not too good (i. e. lean).</definition>
        </example>
